{"availability":"available","full":"optiquant/whatfirst-small","name":"whatfirst-small","description":"A smaller version of what-first.com: Offline small-model task prioritizer for the HF Build Small hackathon - Gradio + llama.cpp (Qwen2.5-VL-3B). A clean-room reimagining of the what-first.com scoring engine, by the same team, June 2026.","category":"Productivity","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-07T20:46:47Z","updated":"2026-06-19T05:57:11Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/build-small-hackathon/whatfirst-small","topics":["gradio","llama-cpp","llm","local-ai","qwen","vision-language-model"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/build-small-hackathon/whatfirst-small","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:04.230Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:04.230Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:04.230Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T22:34:04.230Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Dump everything on your mind — get back what to do first, with the math shown.","Deciding what to do first is a real, daily problem — and most \"AI to-do\" apps answer it with a black box. This one keeps the AI where it earns its keep (turning vague human language into structured fields) and makes the prioritization itself legible: two competing scores (do-it-now vs. de-risk-first), an urgency curve that explodes as a deadline nears, a quick-win boost for short, high-impact tasks, and deadlines treated as a hard constraint rather than a number folded into a blob.","The problem — and the prioritization approach — come from what-first.com, a full web app the same team built in June 2026. There, a frontier cloud model (Claude) does the language work — reading your tasks and proposing their impact, readiness, and effort — and a deterministic engine ranks them. This entry asks a smaller question: can a 3B model running offline on a laptop do that same language work? The ranking engine here is a clean-room Python reimplementation with its own tests, not a copy of the original."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/optiquant/whatfirst-small/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e854df3a60e2047f522990a73e96c250c40786fb74a04afb31de66fcaadbbd53","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:04.365Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:04.365Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Dump everything on your mind — get back what to do first, with the math shown.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/optiquant/whatfirst-small/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"e854df3a60e2047f522990a73e96c250c40786fb74a04afb31de66fcaadbbd53","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/optiquant/whatfirst-small/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:04.366Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-06-19T05:57:11Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/optiquant/whatfirst-small/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:04.366Z","hash":"e854df3a60e2047f522990a73e96c250c40786fb74a04afb31de66fcaadbbd53","originalBytes":5336,"storedBytes":5336,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["nbsp","model","llama.cpp","what","achievement","demo","engine","first","score.py","small","brain-dump","deterministic","docker","how","language","local","notes","python","scoring","structured","tasks","whatfirst-small","where","absorbs","apache-2.0","app","backyard","bash","box","build","built","cloud","design","each","effort","every","face","field","full","ggml-org","hugging","impact","it.","list","live","localhost","math","number","offline","one","output","photo","prioritization","problem","qwen2.5-vl-3b","qwen2.5-vl-3b-instruct-gguf","ranked","ranks","readiness","run","running","runs","same","story","submission","task","test","tests","to-do","track","try","watch","what-first.com","whatfirst","whatfirst-small-writeup.md","wobbles","work","worked","alike.","answer","any"